  "title": "Federal Government Deep Website Review — September 16–22, 2026",
  "question": "What materially changed across official U.S. federal websites after the latest trustworthy per-family cursors, including quiet changes to authority, discretion, records, eligibility, payment, delivery and operation that matter to established Freedom 250 plotlines?",
  "bluf": "The September 16–22 record shows no single government-wide program. Across executive, financial, industrial, military, health, records, trade, communications and foreign-assistance systems, the common movement is a redistribution of decision rights, access gates, record duties and implementation responsibility. Current atomics include the H-1B pair, ACA registration moratorium, OPM award controls, BIS polysilicon import gate, State records rule, MCC compact entry into force and the Joint Warfighter Evaluation announcement; operating/promote-review receipts include DOE/PJM emergency-power use, Army activation/fielding, DHS assistance authority and an FCC Covered List exclusion. The JWE object was inside the frozen cutoff but recovered after close; its governing memo, implementation, board use and outcomes remain unproved. Proposals, source holds, blocked sites, payments, delivery and observed effects remain separately bounded.",
